0..79 Comment "//! A family applied at a call\'s result converts with itself. A type that reads"
80..161 Comment "//! a call\'s value runs the call first and binds it, so `tm(extend(g))` is `c ←"
162..239 Comment "//! extend(g); tm(c)`; a dependent arrow instantiated at the call `extend(g)`"
240..319 Comment "//! binds it ahead of each code that reads the binder, so the type it yields is"
320..400 Comment "//! written the same way. The shape is a category with families: operations over"
401..473 Comment "//! context extension, laws that apply one operation to another\'s result"
474..553 Comment "//! [Dybjer-1996-internal_type_theory]. The same law stated as a record\'s field"
554..629 Comment "//! reads the record\'s family field by its label in every type it prints. A"
630..708 Comment "//! record holding the family and an operation into it checks the operation at"
709..783 Comment "//! the family it holds , and its operation\'s type prints as the arrow the"
784..812 Comment "//! family\'s argument drops."
813..816 Comment "//!"
817..853 Comment "//! - see: #720 — `useAtExtension`"
854..883 Comment "//! - see: #728 — `fieldAt`"
884..918 Comment "//! - see: #721 — `familyRecord`"
919..953 Comment "//! - see: #736 — `familyRecord`"
954..994 Comment "//! - see: #2751 — `appliedWrittenOut`"
995..1042 Comment "//! - cites: [Dybjer-1996-internal_type_theory]"
1043..1046 Comment "//!"
1047..1158 Comment "//! [Dybjer-1996-internal_type_theory]: https://doi.org/10.1007/3-540-61780-9_66 \"Dybjer, Internal Type Theory\""
